 "notes": "The re-read protocol: exp233's deposit is consumed read-only (the bytes sha256-recorded before any read and re-verified unchanged after; the file is never opened for write). The measured errs, the per-point pass bits and the grid coordinates are the deposit's own quantities, consumed as-is \u2014 ZERO re-simulation on the gate path. The three prediction terms are re-derived per point with the frozen forms IMPORTED verbatim (exp79's v_term/theta_term; exp233's field_term on the field_weights kernel, whose f_worst/worst-cell profile was re-checked against the deposit's field_kernel block) and composed as pred_q = sqrt(eV^2 + eT^2 + ef^2) at full precision; every recomputed term matches the deposit's 2dp stored value, so the re-derivation is the deposit's own arithmetic continued, not a new instrument. Q1 gates the Spearman rank correlation on the house convention (argsort-of-argsort corrcoef, exp79/exp233's own); Q2 gates the writability boundary (pred_q < 6.0 iff err < 6.0) at exp79 TC-G1's 80% clause. Q3 is the pre-registered conditional verdict: QUADRATURE is named only if Q1+Q2 both PASS; if Q1 REFUTES the form stays open; the observed outcome (Q1 PASS, Q2 REFUTE) is the unnamed middle case \u2014 neither pre-named branch fires, so the composition is honestly NOT named and the branch is recorded OPEN with the partial disclosed. Q4's determinism: no RNG on the re-read path, the full derivation run twice in-process and asserted identical, and the cross-process re-run (two fresh invocations) verified byte-identical on the results file pre-commit. The docstring and every other byte of this module above main() are identical to pre-registration commit 1b98432.",
 "finding": "Q1 PASS: the quadrature composition pred_q=sqrt(eV^2+eT^2+ef^2) over the re-derived frozen terms pools at Spearman 0.936 across the 27-point deposited grid (bar 0.90; the max-form's failed 0.700; exp233's non-gating preview 0.933 on the 2dp deposit, 0.936 recomposed from the deposited rounded terms) \u2014 the rank law HOLDS at quadrature; Q2 REFUTE: the writability boundary (pred_q<6.0 iff err<6.0) agrees on 21/27 = 77.8%, under the 80% bar \u2014 all 6 misses are the torus arm at gamma>=4, where the theta-term (11.45) dominates pred_q at 11.45-11.81 while the measured errs sit under the bar (4.80-5.92): quadrature fixed the RANKING, not the boundary, and the residual is the theta-term's torus over-prediction, not the field channel (the max-form posted the same 21/27); Q3: branch OPEN \u2014 the composition is NOT named (NONE \u2014 the unnamed middle case (Q1 PASS, Q2 REFUTE); the naming condition Q1+Q2 is unmet, deposited honestly): the three-channel composition form stays open, with the partial disclosed (the rank law holds at quadrature while the boundary clause fails on the theta term's torus face; the field channel's status is unchanged from exp233's deposit); Q4 PASS: exp233's deposit consumed READ-ONLY (sha256 49762aa86dcb688d0aad0d9d5fa909b35f966dd1bb341cc085d09302f5f69f54 recorded pre-read and byte-unchanged through the re-read), all 27 points' terms re-derived with the imported frozen forms match the deposit's 2dp values (max deviation 0.0049 mV, pure rounding), zero re-simulation (the measured errs are the deposit's), the arithmetic deterministic (in-process double derivation bit-identical; cross-process re-run verified byte-identical pre-commit)."
